The Lonely Soldier by ManInTheBlueSuit

summary:
In the early days of the war, Hordak takes a desperate gamble to create a new type of soldier, one that can withstand any punishment, recover from any wound. 
But life and death are fundamental constants that should not be treated lightly, and recovering from any grievous injury requires nutrition - and these new soldiers have a hunger that is not easily sated.


